 how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone- pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-21T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Douglas, CO; Denver, CO; Boulder, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Weld, CO; Jefferson, CO; Adams, CO; Broomfield, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c826c19e1605803e4deefdec974c68b006bd22c3.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c826c19e1605803e4deefdec974c68b006bd22c3.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-21T18:30:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 211830 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1230 PM MDT Fri Aug 21 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Hot today with high temperatures pushing 100F over portions of the plains and I-25 Corridor. - High-based afternoon and evening showers/storms/virga producing gusty microburst winds, with a few strong to severe storms possible for the far eastern plains t","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-20T19:47:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Friday... Very warm temperatures today will warm even further to near record levels for Friday. Humidity recovery tonight will be good over the eastern plains and high mountain valleys, but only moderate at best in the foothills and thermal belts of the mountains. Under Friday's heat, minimum RH will drop into the 12-18% range over most areas, but 20-26% over th","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ftl01","station_name":"Fort Lupton","distance_km":